  "meta": {"utc": "2026-10-16T21:07:25Z", "host": "debian", "kernel": "7.1.8+deb13-rt-amd64", "cpu_model": "Intel(R) Core(TM) Ultra 9 285H", "cpus": "16", "governor": "performance x16", "loadavg_start": "23.05 18.18 15.48 1/2893 2063027", "git_rev": "098e8ae", "git_dirty": "true", "bus_impl": "dbus-daemon (private, tests/harness/run-isolated.sh)", "python": "Python 3.13.5", "build": "release", "label": "vte-fake-wasm-2", "reader": "daemon:<repo>/target/release/gorca", "backend": "voicego", "repeats": "1", "samples_per_series": "1200", "l2_trials": "400", "quick": "false", "loadavg_end": "23.05 18.18 15.48 2/2893 2063024", "reader_env": "GORCA_M6=1 GORCA_M6_STRICT=1 GORCA_V2_SECS=10", "gates": "L1/L3/L4/K1 p99<=15ms, L2 p99<=5ms, lost==0; median over repeats", "reader_args": "--impersonate-orca", "ext_dir": "none", "extensions": "none", "note0": "V1: emit of the last VTE frame to the SPEAK of the output it carried; includes the 30 ms settle, one GetText of the python fake app and the speech lane (gate: settle <= 30 ms wall + 5 ms gorca)", "note1": "VT: 9686 keys (typed 8550, BackSpace 357, Left 337, Right 337, Enter 105); every one spoken exactly once, nothing else", "note2": "VH: typing, Tab, Left, Ctrl+Left, Ctrl+A/E, BackSpace, Enter, Up/Down history, Ctrl+C, a 20-line listing", "note3": "V2: three floods of 10 s each (60 % unattended, then typed keys) at 60 frames/s on a 60x240 screen (cat: 150 distinct lines per frame, yes: 600, make: 40); gates: cpu < 60 % of a core, SIOCINQ p99 < 1 MiB (ss -xpn on the reader's sockets every 50 ms), no broker disconnect (the reader answers after every flood)", "note4": "V3: Ctrl+C key emit to the speech cancel at the server (the L2 path), then the app stops the flood and prints ^C and the prompt; v3_stale counts flood lines spoken after the key", "note5": "probe #11 (type; before: type \"V\", type \"y\") wanted \"3\", heard [-45.4ms \"V\", -23.5ms \"y\", +0.5ms \"3\", +58.7ms \"Sorry, try again.\\n[sudo] password for me:\"]", "note6": "VR: numpad review of a held terminal screen; vr_ipc_calls are application calls during the series (gate 0)", "note7": "big screen Left (row): wanted \"2\", heard []", "note8": "VF: a pager page, a cursor row moved by Down, an htop-style repaint, an edit on a full screen, a 60x200 screen in ASCII and Cyrillic (caret mid-screen, Left)", "note9": "VB: a second terminal floods at 60 frames/s while the focused one is typed in; the key echo and the shell echo of the focused one are the only speech", "note10": "VW: output after Alt+Tab into the terminal before any key; lost per case [0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0] (order, FOCUSED lag, bounce: [(\"activate_first\", 0, false), (\"focus_first\", 0, false), (\"focus_first\", 8, false), (\"activate_first\", 8, false), (\"focus_first\", 8, true), (\"focus_first\", 160, false), (\"focus_first\", 400, false)]); latency is frame emit to SPEAK as in V1"},
